WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:07.186
&gt;&gt;&gt; But first, here is my take.

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:08.654
In his important book the third

00:00:08.787 --> 00:00:10.723
wave, Samuel Huntington pointed

00:00:10.856 --> 00:00:12.358
out the division among the

00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:15.194
ruling elite is a key sign of

00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:18.564
weakness in authoritarian

00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:18.897
regimes.

00:00:19.031 --> 00:00:19.832
When members of the

00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:20.632
establishment break with the

00:00:20.766 --> 00:00:22.234
system, it triggers a larger set

00:00:22.368 --> 00:00:23.836
of changes.

00:00:23.936 --> 00:00:25.204
Conversely, when you do not see

00:00:25.337 --> 00:00:27.206
such defections, it means the

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:28.407
autocrat will probably be able

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.109
to survive.

00:00:30.242 --> 00:00:33.278
Syrian dictator bashar Al Assad

00:00:33.412 --> 00:00:36.648
is one example of this principle

00:00:36.782 --> 00:00:36.982
at work.

00:00:37.116 --> 00:00:42.454
So how would be apply to that

00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:43.856
Russia today.

00:00:43.856 --> 00:00:46.125
Prigozhin's failed attempt, but

00:00:46.258 --> 00:00:47.359
Vladimir Putin was able to snuff

00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:48.827
it out within a day or two.

00:00:48.961 --> 00:00:51.864
It appears that prigozhin got no

00:00:51.997 --> 00:00:54.633
public support from any key

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:55.300
figure in the Kremlin which

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:57.036
could be why he ended his March

00:00:57.169 --> 00:00:58.804
on Moscow.

00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:00.739
Putin has spent much of his

00:01:00.873 --> 00:01:02.741
tenure crushing dissent from

00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:05.411
liberals and now subduing his

00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:10.015
challengers on the nationalist

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:10.315
side.

00:01:10.449 --> 00:01:12.684
Power struggles takes place in a

00:01:12.818 --> 00:01:14.887
black box.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.022
As the lines to Winston

00:01:17.156 --> 00:01:27.399
Churchill go it is comparable to

00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:28.133
a fight under a rug and when he

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:33.439
sees the bones fly out, now we

00:01:33.572 --> 00:01:34.673
see prigozhin's bones.

00:01:34.807 --> 00:01:36.408
What is not a matter of

00:01:36.542 --> 00:01:37.910
regulation is the state of

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:38.444
Russian society.

00:01:38.577 --> 00:01:40.712
I've been stunned by unstatistic

00:01:40.846 --> 00:01:43.916
ever since a read it.

00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:44.616
A 15-year-old Russian male today

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.922
has the same life expectancy as

00:01:50.055 --> 00:01:50.989
a 15-year-old male in Haiti.

00:01:51.123 --> 00:01:52.524
Russia is one of the world's

00:01:52.658 --> 00:01:53.926
richest countries in terms of

00:01:53.926 --> 00:01:56.261
normal resources and it is an

00:01:56.395 --> 00:01:57.529
urbanized industrialized society

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.099
with levels of education and

00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:01.467
literacy comparable to and

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.335
perhaps even exceeding Europe

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:05.437
yap countries.

00:02:05.571 --> 00:02:09.208
This analysis comes from an

00:02:09.341 --> 00:02:11.944
August 2022 working paper by the

00:02:11.944 --> 00:02:16.081
scholar who has long studied

00:02:16.215 --> 00:02:16.482
demography.

00:02:16.615 --> 00:02:18.283
He pointed out that for three

00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.053
decades Russia has been de

00:02:21.186 --> 00:02:21.453
populating.

00:02:21.587 --> 00:02:25.958
From 2013 to 2015, deaths have

00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:26.291
outpaced births.

00:02:26.425 --> 00:02:27.960
But this trend is one we see in

00:02:28.026 --> 00:02:29.294
many industrialized countries.

00:02:29.428 --> 00:02:31.497
What stands out in Russia is its

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.197
mortality rate.

00:02:32.331 --> 00:02:33.999
Using the world health

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.201
organization's data in 2019,

00:02:36.335 --> 00:02:38.103
before any effects from covid or

00:02:38.237 --> 00:02:40.339
the war, the world health

00:02:40.472 --> 00:02:42.641
organization estimated a

00:02:42.774 --> 00:02:43.976
15-year-old boy in Russia could

00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:47.980
expect to live another 53.7

00:02:48.013 --> 00:02:48.947
years which is about the same as

00:02:49.148 --> 00:02:51.283
a Haitian and below the life

00:02:51.416 --> 00:02:55.988
expectancies for males in Yemen,

00:02:55.988 --> 00:02:58.123
Mali, South Sudan and males

00:02:58.257 --> 00:02:59.491
about the same age could live

00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:01.460
seven years longer than

00:03:01.593 --> 00:03:01.994
Russians.

00:03:01.994 --> 00:03:03.228
Education usually correlated

00:03:03.362 --> 00:03:06.765
with good health but not in

00:03:06.899 --> 00:03:07.099
Russia.

00:03:07.232 --> 00:03:08.667
Shockingly Russia is a country

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.702
with first world educational

00:03:10.836 --> 00:03:12.204
levels and fourth world

00:03:12.337 --> 00:03:14.406
mortality rates for its working

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.474
age population.

00:03:15.607 --> 00:03:17.176
He then digs deeper into the

00:03:17.309 --> 00:03:18.810
educational attainments and

00:03:18.944 --> 00:03:21.280
finds that the mystery deepens.

00:03:21.413 --> 00:03:23.115
With huge numbers of well

00:03:23.248 --> 00:03:24.216
trained people, especially in

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:27.619
the sciences, Russia performs

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:28.787
miserably in the knowledge

00:03:28.921 --> 00:03:29.121
economy.

00:03:29.254 --> 00:03:31.657
Much worse than did the soviet

00:03:32.024 --> 00:03:34.026
union.

00:03:34.026 --> 00:03:36.028
In 2019, Russia ranked behind

00:03:36.028 --> 00:03:38.030
Austria in international patent

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.032
applications despite having 16

00:03:40.032 --> 00:03:41.500
times the population.

00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:44.203
Today it ranks alongside Alabama

00:03:44.336 --> 00:03:47.272
in U.S. Patents, the gold

00:03:47.406 --> 00:03:48.273
standard for companies

00:03:48.407 --> 00:03:48.674
everywhere.

00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:50.042
Despite having almost 30 times

00:03:50.108 --> 00:03:53.345
the population of Alabama.

00:03:53.478 --> 00:03:54.646
All of these numbers will likely

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.048
get much worse given the

00:03:56.114 --> 00:03:58.083
hundreds of thousands of likely

00:03:58.217 --> 00:04:02.754
well trained urban educated

00:04:02.888 --> 00:04:04.056
Russians who fled the country

00:04:04.089 --> 00:04:07.159
after its aggression against

00:04:07.292 --> 00:04:07.492
Ukraine.

00:04:07.626 --> 00:04:08.160
What explains the stunning

00:04:08.293 --> 00:04:09.428
mismatch in Russia?

00:04:09.561 --> 00:04:12.564
A new book by the scholar

00:04:12.698 --> 00:04:15.567
Alexander edkin, Russia against

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:16.935
modernity, makes the case that

00:04:17.069 --> 00:04:20.872
Putin has created a state that

00:04:21.006 --> 00:04:24.376
gets revenues by exacting

00:04:24.509 --> 00:04:26.078
natural resources and fulfilled

00:04:26.111 --> 00:04:28.113
none of the functions of a

00:04:28.247 --> 00:04:30.249
modern state in terms of

00:04:30.382 --> 00:04:33.185
providing welfare for people.

00:04:33.318 --> 00:04:35.053
Corruption is in this regime

00:04:35.187 --> 00:04:36.488
noting that post soviet Russia

00:04:36.622 --> 00:04:38.624
has seen the fastest rise in

00:04:38.757 --> 00:04:40.425
inequality anywhere in the

00:04:40.559 --> 00:04:40.726
world.

00:04:40.859 --> 00:04:42.728
After the protests against him

00:04:42.861 --> 00:04:46.632
in 2011 and 2012, which enraged

00:04:46.765 --> 00:04:49.601
Putin blamed on then secretary

00:04:49.735 --> 00:04:50.969
Hillary Clinton, the Russian

00:04:51.103 --> 00:04:52.804
state became even more

00:04:52.938 --> 00:04:53.205
anti-modern.

00:04:53.338 --> 00:04:56.408
For Putin's regime, the west

00:04:56.541 --> 00:04:59.478
represents forces of social,

00:04:59.611 --> 00:05:00.178
economic and political

00:05:00.312 --> 00:05:02.114
modernization that could infect

00:05:02.147 --> 00:05:02.347
Russia.

00:05:02.481 --> 00:05:04.583
In his speech as he launched the

00:05:04.716 --> 00:05:08.787
war in Ukraine, Putin accused

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.122
the United States of destroying

00:05:10.122 --> 00:05:11.623
Russia's traditional values and

00:05:11.757 --> 00:05:13.558
impose new ones on it, which,

00:05:13.692 --> 00:05:16.695
directly lead to degradation and

00:05:16.828 --> 00:05:17.663
degeneration because they are

00:05:17.796 --> 00:05:20.132
contrary to human nature.

00:05:20.132 --> 00:05:22.134
For Putin, modernizing Russia

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.636
would create a more active civil

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.638
society with greater demands for

00:05:26.772 --> 00:05:28.373
better health care, more

00:05:28.507 --> 00:05:29.541
opportunities for ordinary

00:05:29.675 --> 00:05:31.410
citizens and a less klepto

00:05:31.543 --> 00:05:32.444
crattic state.

00:05:32.577 --> 00:05:34.346
And so he advocates a

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:35.113
traditional Russia.

00:05:35.247 --> 00:05:38.216
Which celebrates religion,

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.520
traditional morality and

00:05:41.653 --> 00:05:43.722
xenophobia and strick gender

00:05:44.156 --> 00:05:44.923
conformity, of course.

00:05:45.057 --> 00:05:48.160
What does this all add up to?

00:05:48.293 --> 00:05:48.593
I'm not sure.

00:05:48.727 --> 00:05:50.896
But it is fair to say that

